# Agential Skill Rules (by Talha Irfan / codedits)

Whenever working on this codebase:
1. **Persistent Memory (`context.md`)**:
   - Check if `context.md` exists at project root to instantly reload project context and past decisions.
   - Update `context.md` after agreeing on visual decisions or completing milestones.
2. **Inspiration-First UI Rule**:
   - Before building any new web app/frontend UI, first search for 2-3 relevant real-world apps/web apps in the same category so the output does not look random.
3. **Mandatory Frontend Kickoff**:
   - When starting new UI without design specs, ask 3-4 structured questions: (1) Theme, (2) Hero CTA, (3) Density, (4) Pacing.
   - BYPASS RULE: If the user already provided visual preferences/specs, or if editing an existing project, DO NOT ask questions. Build immediately.
4. **Framer Clean Design, Section Architecture & Framer Motion**:
   - Strictly NO rainbow gradients. Subtle single-color atmospheric light glows are encouraged for depth.
   - Minimal roundness: Use `6px` to `8px` for buttons/CTAs and `8px` to `12px` for cards. Never use pill capsules (`9999px`) or bubble cards.
   - Clean fonts only: Always use `Plus Jakarta Sans`, `Manrope`, `Poppins`, or `Inter`. Never funky or novelty fonts.
   - Elite navbars and heroes: Prioritize sticky, blurred navbars and authoritative, spacious heroes.
   - Section Architecture (100vh–140vh Desktop, Fluid Mobile): Architect webapps into distinct storytelling sections with one signature component per section. Desktop scale: 100vh–140vh for sticky reveals. If static, use natural fluid height with generous padding (py-24 to py-32) or 80vh-100vh (never add 140vh empty void). Always use `min-height`, never fixed `height`. Keep mobile fluid (`min-height: auto` or `100svh`/`100dvh`).
   - Framer Motion Dynamic Animation (Never Let UI Feel Dead): Prefer Framer Motion (`framer-motion`/`motion/react`). Use smooth slide-up text reveals (`opacity: 0, y: 24` -> `1, 0`), scroll reveals (`whileInView`), and staggered cards (`staggerChildren: 0.1`). Always animate strictly GPU properties (`transform`, `opacity`).
5. **Paced Feature Delivery**: Deliver in cohesive, high-craft chunks (e.g. Navbar + complete Hero stage). If a full page is explicitly requested, build the complete architecture without cutting corners or stalling prematurely.
6. **Low-CPU Optimization & Bulletproof Backend Architecture**:
   - Frontend: Write 60fps web code. Eliminate DOM layout thrashing, animate exclusively using CSS `transform` and `opacity`, debounce typing by 200-300ms, and use passive listeners.
   - Backend: (1) Boot-time fail-fast env validation (Zod/Pydantic BaseSettings), (2) Anti-IDOR scoped queries (always scope by verified userId/tenantId), (3) Zero N+1 queries & mandatory pagination limits (max 50-100), (4) Atomic transactions for multi-step writes, (5) Strict schemas (.strict() / extra="forbid"), (6) Sanitized errors with correlation IDs.
7. **Mandatory Post-Edit Review Pass**: Immediately after editing any file, re-read the diff to verify all imports, tags, brackets, and caller interfaces are completely intact.
